project_description:
The purpose of the proposed A/R CDM project activity is to realize multiple socio-economic and environmental benefits (climate change mitigation. local community development. biodiversity conservation and soil erosion control) through restoring forest vegetation on degraded lands. Specific project objectives include:
- to sequester carbon dioxide through reforestation on degraded lands in headwater areas of the Pearl River;
- to control soil and water erosion and land degradation in the selected project areas;
- to enhance biodiversity conservation by increasing forest cover and nature habitat connectivity;
- to generate income for the local farmers and promote the local community development.

To contribute to the local sustainable development. the proposed A/R CDM project activity aims to:
- Sequester carbon dioxide and mitigating climate change;
- Enhance biodiversity conservation by increasing the connectivity of forests adjacent to nature reserves;
- Improve soil and water conservation in the upper reaches of the Yangtze River;
- Generate income for local communities.

