project_description:
The project will help mitigate deforestation through the promotion of rational land occupancy and use methods. Thus. 10.000 ha will be placed under rational management of which 1.300 ha will be earmarked for agro-forestry; 6 million trees will be planted. deforestation will be reduced by 30% and one million tons of CO2 will be stored by 2017. The project will also produce 3000 tons of cassava. construct 3 living centers and 500 m2 of trading infrastructure. rehabilitate 3 health centers and 3 schools and rehabilitate 50 km of feeder roads.

The project will be implemented in four phases:
1. Sites research and participative cartography. launch of an information management system (collection. analysis and dissemination of activities and the launch of the MRV system);
2. Installation of basic infrastructure;
3. Implementation of agroforestry activities;
4. Implementation of activities targeting commercialization. distribution and transformation

The overall objective of the project is to reduce deforestation and poverty in the region. The project will support the development of agroforestry activities. through:
- the reforestation of 3500ha of areas used for agricultural and wood exploitation purposes;
- the creation of cooperatives to help local people in the commercialisation of their products;
- the rehabilitation of technical. social and economical infrastructures
- the development of nurseries and agroforestry plantations
It will help local populations to shift towards more sustainable activities. and to increase their income.

The project will allow the establishment of 187 Jatropha curcas plantations covering an area of 14.000 hectares (ha) of mostly degraded soils. More specifically. the project objectives are:
- Sequestration of carbon dioxide (CO2) by the cultivation of Jatropha curcas;
- Regeneration of degraded soils and protect them against erosion;
- Empowerment of local communities to develop sustainable agro-forestry practices. and
- Provision of an alternate livelihood potential for local communities.

The Pax Natura project is an avoided deforestation (REDD+) project on private lands located in the Central Volcanic Mountain Range of Costa Rica.
The project aims to:
- Mitigate carbon dioxide emissions. and protect biodiversity and water resources in forest areas bordering national parks by reducing deforestation;
- Contribute to efforts to prevent climate change;
- Participate in maintaining the biological integrity of the landscape in the Central Volcanic Range Conservation Area.

