project_description:
Chile’s landscape in the south of Santiago is known as “secano interior” (interior dry-land area). Once a forested area. it was cleared for crop production in the 19th century and land became highly degraded.
Fundación Chile works to develop a model of forest securitization that would promote:
- Improvement in the productivity of degraded lands through reforestation;
- Participation of land owners to generate economies of scale for land restoration activities;
- Incorporation of state-of-the-art silviculture for improving forest growth.

Project is planting only two types of tree species. both of which are non-native. Project is being implemented with assistance from Chilean forestry companies. Fundacion Chile. a Chilean non-profit. created SIF (project proponent) as a private company to manage the leasing of private lands for plantation forestry. The forestry companies implementing the plantation planting and management  are FSC certified.

