project_description:
The Lachuá Carbon Project is a planned early REDD+ initiative around the Lake Lachuá National Park (Parque Nacional Laguna Lachuá; PNLL) in the North-West of Petén department. The proposed activities are:
- providing alternative income generation activities;
- sustainable forest management; 
- control and vigilance;
- ecotourism.
 This would avoid emissions of 2.587.356 tonnes C02e over the 30-year project lifetime.

